A sliding window counter in Redis: the counts of the current and the previous minute, weighted by how far we are into the current minute. Each request costs two INCR calls and one EXPIRE in one MULTI. A token bucket would need a Lua script. The sliding window is simpler and within about 1% of exact.

```ts
export async function hit(key: string, limit: number, now = Date.now()) {
  const minute = Math.floor(now / 60_000)
  const [current, previous] = await redis.multi()
    .incr(`${key}:${minute}`).get(`${key}:${minute - 1}`)
    .expire(`${key}:${minute}`, 120).exec()
  const weight = 1 - (now % 60_000) / 60_000
  return Number(current) + Number(previous ?? 0) * weight <= limit
}
```
